# The corpus is compared byte for byte.
#
# `tests/programs.rs` diffs a case's output against its companion file, trimming
# only whitespace at the very end so that a missing final newline is not a
# failure. Everything inside the file counts — a `.report` renders carets by
# padding with spaces, so a harness that normalised them could not tell a
# misaligned caret from a correct one. That only works if the companion file has
# the same line endings everywhere, so the files are pinned rather than the
# comparison loosened. Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` hands a Windows
# checkout CRLF and three cases fail before anything is even run.
#
# The `.qn` files are pinned for the same reason from the other end: they are
# the source a report's carets are measured against.
tests/cases/*.qn text eol=lf
tests/cases/*.out text eol=lf
tests/cases/*.err text eol=lf
tests/cases/*.report text eol=lf
examples/*.qn text eol=lf
